---
description: When the user asks to break, pen-test, security-test, or audit a live site with credentials, follow the break-audit skill.
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user supplies a website URL plus username/password and asks to break the site, find vulnerabilities, security issues, functional breaks, or UX problems:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/break-audit/SKILL.md` and follow it exactly before reporting.
2. Discover the API with `python3 .cursor/skills/break-audit/scripts/discover_api.py --site <url>`.
3. Run `python3 .cursor/skills/break-audit/scripts/probe_api.py` with `--site`, `--api`, `--email`, `--password`, and `--out probe-findings.json`. Add `--destructive` only if the user explicitly opted in.
4. Complete browser phases (auth, XSS/`javascript:` URLs, functional, UX) using the checklist in `.cursor/skills/break-audit/CHECKLIST.md`.
5. Write `break-audit-run.json` (never include the password) and execute:
   `python3 .cursor/skills/break-audit/scripts/validate_run.py break-audit-run.json`
6. Show findings only after that command prints `OK`. `FAIL` means the skill was skipped or incomplete.
